# Claude Code agent worktrees (isolated per-agent git repos, not project content)
.claude/

# Defense in depth: backend/.gitignore already covers backend/.env (the
# only .env that exists today), but that only protects a file placed
# there specifically. A repo-root rule means a .env dropped anywhere
# else later is never one accidental `git add -A` away from being
# committed for real.
.env
*.env
!.env.example
